license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A proof-of-concept study of counter-evidence loss in RAG. Across six
  synthetic claims, correctness fell from 6/6 to 0/6 when answer-changing
  evidence remained available but was not exposed to the generator, while
  RAGAS Faithfulness stayed at or above 0.917 and a reference-free
  sufficiency judge rated 18/18 contexts sufficient.
